#, no-wrap
msgid "Single-threaded\n"
msgstr "Berutas tunggal\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Computational requirements {#computational-requirements}"
msgstr "Kebutuhan komputasi {#computational-requirements}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the memory and time cost for Pauli propagation routines generally scale with the size to which the evolved operator is allowed to grow.\n"
msgstr "Baik biaya memori maupun waktu untuk rutin Pauli propagation umumnya berskala dengan ukuran yang boleh dicapai operator yang berevolusi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`propagate_through_rotation_gates()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates\"): As the Pauli operator is propagated in the Pauli basis under the action of a sequence of $N$ Pauli rotation gates of an $M$-qubit circuit, the number of terms will grow as $\\mathcal{O}(2^N)$ towards a maximum of $4^M$ unique Pauli components. To control memory usage, the operator is truncated after application of each gate, which introduces some error proportional to the magnitudes of the truncated terms’ coefficients. The memory requirements are linear in the size of the evolved operator, and runtime scales linearly in both the operator size and the number of gates.\n"
msgstr "[`propagate_through_rotation_gates()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates\"): Saat operator Pauli dipropagasikan dalam basis Pauli di bawah aksi urutan $N$ gate rotasi Pauli dari circuit $M$-qubit, jumlah suku akan tumbuh sebesar $\\mathcal{O}(2^N)$ menuju maksimum $4^M$ komponen Pauli yang unik. Untuk mengendalikan pemakaian memori, operator dipotong setelah penerapan tiap gate, yang menimbulkan sedikit error sebanding dengan besar koefisien suku yang dipotong. Kebutuhan memorinya linear terhadap ukuran operator yang berevolusi, dan waktu eksekusinya berskala linear terhadap ukuran operator maupun jumlah gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`propagate_through_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator\"): Conjugates one operator in the Pauli basis by another by greedily accumulating terms in the sum, $\\sum_{i,j,k}G^{\\dagger}_iO_jG_k$, where $i,j,k$ are sparse indices over the Pauli basis. This implementation sorts the coefficients in each operator by descending magnitude then searches the 3D index space for the terms with the largest coefficients, starting with the origin $(0,0,0)$, and accumulating $(i,j,k)$ triplets up to a specified cutoff. The time spent searching can often be made negligible by increasing the search step size in $(i,j,k)$ space, which provides a cubic speedup for this subroutine. In our profiling, significant time can be spent sorting the operators and performing Pauli multiplication to generate the terms in the new operator.\n"
msgstr "[`propagate_through_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator\"): Mengonjugasikan satu operator dalam basis Pauli dengan operator lain dengan mengakumulasi suku-suku secara greedy dalam jumlah, $\\sum_{i,j,k}G^{\\dagger}_iO_jG_k$, dengan $i,j,k$ adalah indeks sparse atas basis Pauli. Implementasi ini mengurutkan koefisien di tiap operator berdasarkan besar secara menurun lalu mencari di ruang indeks 3D suku-suku dengan koefisien terbesar, dimulai dari titik asal $(0,0,0)$, dan mengakumulasi triplet $(i,j,k)$ sampai batas tertentu. Waktu yang dipakai untuk pencarian sering bisa dibuat dapat diabaikan dengan memperbesar ukuran langkah pencarian di ruang $(i,j,k)$, yang memberi percepatan kubik untuk subrutin ini. Dalam profiling kami, waktu yang cukup besar bisa terpakai untuk mengurutkan operator dan melakukan perkalian Pauli guna menghasilkan suku-suku di operator baru.\n"

